# Part B — Implementation Specification (for one-shot generation)

> Authoritative, self-contained build spec. Ground truth is `rf_tracer_spec.md` (RTL-corroborated). Reference artifacts (in `~/Downloads`, `~/Pictures`) are the conformance oracle:
> `elf2dbgid.py`, `rcl_generic_tx_burst_lp_em_cc2745r10_q1_nortos_llvm.out` (ELF), its dbgid `..._dbgid.h` + `_dbgid_pbe_generic.h`, `tx_burst_example.sal` (Saleae capture), `tx_burst_example_decoded.txt` (golden decode).
>
> **Deliverable / scope:** the **logic-analyzer backend** (sample ingest → deframe → packet decode → dbgid resolve) **+ pipe to Wireshark and stdout**. RF-tracer logs must appear in Wireshark **identically to ITM logs** — same `||` payload, same `tilogger_dissector.lua`, same columns. Only the *backend* is new; the presentation layer is shared with the existing ITM/UART path. The golden `.txt` is a **correctness oracle** (it happens to be the old FPGA-GUI format) — used to verify decoded content, **not** a format to reproduce. Retention/tail/sampler-orchestration are secondary.

## 11. Wire format (RTL ground truth)

### 11.1 Physical layer
- Single GPIO `rfctrc_out`. **Idle high.** Clock `clk_rfctrc` = 24 MHz (some variants 48 MHz → `--divide-time-by-2`).
- **12-bit frame**, MSB drives the pin first:
  - bit 11 (first): **start = 1** (active-high, *not* UART active-low)
  - bits 10:1: **10-bit data word, MSB first**
  - bit 0 (last): **0** (trailing/stop-like)
- Default prescaler → **500 ns/frame** = 2 MHz word rate = 20 Mbit/s payload. `frame_duration = (ser_prescal+1)*12` clk cycles.
- Deframe: recover frame period from start-pulse edges (M2.2), place bit centers (fractional accumulator, ~20.83 samp/bit @ 500 MS/s), read the 12 bits, lift `word10 = frame_bits[10:1]`.
- **Confirmed deframe params** (from the `tx_burst_example.sal` Async-Serial analyzer that produced the golden decode): it is a **standard inverted async-serial UART** — 24 Mbaud, **10 data bits, MSB-first, 1 start, 1 stop, no parity, signal inverted**. So M2.3 is a textbook inverted-UART 10-bit word extractor (start=falling edge after inversion); the RTL "idle-high/active-high start" reconciles with this via the inverted probe. Default `--invert` on; verify NOP decodes to `0x000` and CRC-5 passes.

### 11.2 10-bit word layout
Every word: `word[9:8] = chx_id`, `word[7:0] = payload`. Classify by masks (from `PacketParser.cpp`):

| Word | Detect (on 10-bit `w`) | Fields |
|---|---|---|
| **NOP / idle** | `chx_id==0 && payload==0` (`w==0x000`) | none — drop |
| **Overflow NOP** | `chx_id==0 && (w & 0x00E)!=0` | `w[3:1]` = per-channel overflow (bit3=ch3, 2=ch2, 1=ch1) |
| **TS-MSB (ch0)** | `chx_id==0 && (w & 0x020)!=0` (bit5=1) | `w[4]`=ts_en, `w[0]`=timestamp-counter MSB (seqnum[0]) |
| **SOP** | `(w & 0x3C0)!=0 && (w & 0x320)==0x000` | `w[7:6]`=channel(1..3), `w[4]`=ts_en, `w[3:0]`=seqnum |
| **EOP** | `(w & 0x320)==0x020` | `w[7:6]`=channel, `w[4:0]`=CRC-5 |
| **DATA/TS** | `chx_id!=0` | `chx_id`=channel(1..3), `payload`=byte |

Note the channel is in `w[7:6]` for SOP/EOP (which carry `chx_id==0` in the top bits) but in `w[9:8]` for DATA words. Route each word to the owning channel's state machine accordingly.

### 11.3 Per-channel packet state machine
Maintain 3 independent SMs (channels 1..3); words interleave on the wire. Sequence per packet:

```
SOP(ch, ts_en, seq)
  → if ts_en: DATA→PS_TSH (ts_delta high byte), DATA→PS_TSL (low byte)
  → DATA→PS_HDR  (payload = dbgid, 3..255)
  → DATA× par_cnt: alternating PS_DATAH/PS_DATAL, each pair = one 16-bit param, high byte first
  → EOP(ch, crc5)   // terminates; par_cnt = number of 16-bit words collected (≤4)
```
- dbgid 0–2 reserved (0=debug, 1=timestamp, 2=sim-end) — handle/skip, don't dispatch as logs.
- Params: collect the 16-bit words `par[0..par_cnt)`. **Width comes from the dbgid** (§12): 32-bit args (negative argCount) consume two words, low half first → `arg = par[i] | (par[i+1]<<16)`; 16-bit args (positive argCount) are one word each. Validate `par_cnt` matches the dbgid's expected count.
- seqnum wraps at 16; use to detect dropped packets per channel.

### 11.4 CRC-5
- **CRC-5-USB**, init `0x1F`. Accumulate over payload bytes **from SOP inclusive** through all TS/HDR/DATA words (`next_crc5_d8` on `word[7:0]`), then the 3 MSBs of EOP (`next_crc5_d3` on `word[7:5]`); the transmitted 5-bit CRC sits in `EOP[4:0]`. Re-running the CRC over the received CRC field yields residue `0x00` on a good packet.
- Implement as the 256-entry LUT `crc = lut[data ^ (crc<<3)] & 0x1F` (matches `pCrc5Lut`). **Verify the impl against the golden vectors (§17), not by hand.** CRC-fail → count as health metric, drop packet, do not emit.

### 11.5 Timestamp reconstruction
- 16-bit counter at 24 MHz ÷ 12 = **2 MHz** (0.5 µs/tick). Per packet, TSH/TSL carry a 16-bit snapshot **delta**.
- ch0 TS-MSB word carries `ts_counter[15]`; use it to keep the running MSB synced across rollover.
- Merge delta with `lastTimestamp` upper bits; **rollover: add `0x10000` if the new value is >2000 behind** `lastTimestamp` (matches `PacketParser.cpp`). Then `micros = value / 2` (÷2 again if `--divide-time-by-2`). Format `HH:MM:SS.uuuuuu`. Also keep raw ticks for the pcap timestamp.

## 12. dbgid database (`elf2dbgid` output)

Build step (owned by TI's tool, not us): `elf2dbgid extract <app.out> -o <app>_dbgid.h`. Decoder loads one or more such files.

**`DBG_DEF` line** — 8 fields, exact separators `(`, `, `, …, `, "`, `", "`, `", `, `)`:
```
DBG_DEF(DBGID_<file>_<line>, <dbgid>, DBGCH<ch>, <argCount>, "<fmt>", "<file>", <line>)
```
| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 0 | literal `DBG_DEF` (else skip line) |
| 1 | symbolic name (ignore) |
| 2 | `dbgid` 3..255 (0–2 reserved) |
| 3 | `DBGCH1`/`DBGCH2`/`DBGCH3` → channel 1..3 |
| 4 | `argCount`: **>0 ⇒ that many 16-bit args; <0 ⇒ `|n|` 32-bit args; 0 ⇒ none** |
| 5 | printf format string (C `%` specifiers) |
| 6 | source file (basename after last `/`) |
| 7 | source line number |

- **File-name routing** (matches reference parser): `*_mst.h` → master parser only, `*_slv.h` → slave only, `*.h` → both. Master/slave = the two logical streams (bit 15 of the FPGA 16-bit word; for LA capture, a single die = one stream unless two pins are probed).
- Key the DB on `(channel, dbgid)`. Example rows (from `_dbgid_pbe_generic.h`): `DBG_DEF(DBGID_PBE_RAM_BANK0_ASM_1367, 128, DBGCH2, 0, "…CRC error", "pbe_ram_bank0.asm", 1367)`.
- **printf formatting:** substitute reconstructed args (widths per field 4) into the format string, C-style. Missing/extra args → emit raw + mark malformed, don't panic.

## 13. Decoder architecture (Rust)

Single Cargo workspace, one lib + thin bins. Hot path is allocation-light; use iterators/streaming, no full-capture buffering.

```
tracedecode/
  Cargo.toml
  src/
    lib.rs
    sample.rs     // ingest: raw u8/sample stream (stdin/file) + Saleae .sal reader (§16)
    deframe.rs    // samples → Word stream: clock recovery (M2.2) + framing (M2.3)
    word.rs       // Word, WordKind classify (§11.2)
    crc5.rs       // CRC-5-USB LUT + update; golden-tested
    packet.rs     // 3× per-channel SM (§11.3) → DecodedPacket, CRC check
    timestamp.rs  // TsState reconstruct (§11.5)
    dbgid.rs      // DBG_DEF parser → DbgIdDb keyed (channel,dbgid) (§12)
    record.rs     // DecodedPacket + DbgDef → LogRecord (printf substitution)
    output/
      mod.rs      // Output trait
      stdout.rs   // human text, matches reference decode (§15.1)
      pcap.rs     // DLT_USER0=147, ||-text payload (§15.2)
      extcap.rs   // extcap protocol + fifo (§15.3)
      retain.rs   // dumpcap ring spawn (§15.4)
      tail.rs     // in-mem last-N ring (§15.5)
    synth.rs      // reverse path: DbgIdDb + records → wire → samples (self-test, §16.3)
  bins/ (or [[bin]]): tracedecode (main CLI, §7 surface)
```

**Core types:**
```rust
struct Word { chx_id: u8, payload: u8, raw10: u16 }
enum WordKind { Nop, Overflow(u8), TsMsb{ ts_en: bool, ts_msb: u8 },
                Sop{ ch: u8, ts_en: bool, seq: u8 }, Eop{ ch: u8, crc5: u8 },
                Data{ ch: u8, byte: u8 } }

struct DecodedPacket { channel: u8, dbgid: u8, seq: u8,
                       ts_delta: Option<u16>, params: Vec<u16>, crc_ok: bool }

struct DbgDef { dbgid: u8, channel: u8, arg_count: i32,
                fmt: String, file: String, line: u32 }
struct DbgIdDb { by_key: HashMap<(u8,u8), DbgDef> }   // (channel, dbgid)

struct LogRecord { channel: u8, dbgid: u8, seq: u8,
                   ts_ticks: u64, ts_us: f64, args: Vec<u32>,
                   text: String, def: DbgDef }  // text = fmt % args

trait Output { fn on_record(&mut self, r: &LogRecord); fn on_health(&mut self, h: Health); }
```

**Pipeline (streaming iterators):**
```
samples: impl Iterator<Item=u8>
  → deframe(cfg) : Iterator<Word>
  → classify     : Iterator<WordKind>
  → PacketAssembler (3 SMs + CRC + TsState) : Iterator<DecodedPacket>   // NOPs/overflow/ts-msb consumed as state
  → resolve(&db) : Iterator<LogRecord>
  → for each Output: on_record
```
Backpressure: blocking read on stdin; if any Output is a pipe, a bounded channel + drop-oldest with a health counter (never stall the deframer).

## 14. CLI

See §7 "Decoder CLI." Subcommands compose left-to-right (tilogger-style): one input (`decode`/`replay`/`synth`) + one or more outputs (`stdout`/`wireshark`/`retain`/`tail`). `--dbgid` repeatable. Global deframe flags apply to input.

## 15. Output formats

### 15.1 stdout (human)
Match the **existing `tilogger` stdout**, not the golden `.txt`: default `{I} | {T} | {M} | {L} | {F} | {D}` (identifier, timestamp, module, level, file:line, data). `--format` overrides with the same `{I}{T}{M}{L}{F}{D}` specifiers. Presentation is identical to ITM/UART logs.

### 15.2 Wireshark (pcap + reuse existing dissector) — identical to ITM
- Same path the ITM/UART sinks already use, so RF-tracer logs are indistinguishable from ITM in the UI.
- Classic pcap stream (or pcapng): global header magic `0xA1B2C3D4`, snaplen 256, **linktype `DLT_USER0 = 147`**. One packet per `LogRecord`. Packet ts from `ts_ticks` (µs).
- Payload = UTF-8, **`||`-delimited**, byte-identical to what `tilogger` emits so `tilogger_dissector.lua` works **unchanged**:
  `alias || ts_local(.9f) || opcode || module || level || file || line || text`
  Field mapping for trace records: `alias`=source (e.g. `rftrc`/`--alias`); `opcode`=`LOG_OPCODE_FORMATED_TEXT`; `module`=`DBGCH<n>` (channel); `level`=from dbgid if present else `INFO`; `file`,`line`,`text` from dbgid + args.
- Transport: **extcap** (cross-platform) preferred; `--pipe` named-pipe/fifo fallback mirrors current `tilogger`.

### 15.3 extcap
Implement `--extcap-interfaces`, `--extcap-dlts` (DLT 147), `--extcap-config`, `--capture --fifo <path> --extcap-interface <if>`. On `--capture`, write the pcap stream (15.2) to the fifo.

### 15.4 retain / 15.5 tail
`retain` spawns `dumpcap -b files:N -b filesize:X` on the pcap stream. `tail` keeps an in-mem ring of last-N `LogRecord`, prints on demand / continuously; no Wireshark.

## 16. Input

### 16.1 Raw samples
`unitsize=1`, 1 byte/sample; the `rfctrc_out` line is `--channel` (bit index). stdin (live, from `sigrok-cli … -O binary`) or a file (`replay`).

### 16.2 Saleae `.sal` reader (confirmed against `tx_burst_example.sal`)
`.sal` = ZIP archive containing `meta.json` + one `digital-<N>.bin` per captured channel.
- **Trace pin = digital channel 4** (`digital-4.bin`; meta row "MST:TRC"). Channel 5 = "Cluster: TRC" (the slave/cluster stream). `--channel` selects; default 4.
- `digital-<N>.bin` is Saleae's **transition-list** format (initial level + list of edge timestamps), *not* raw samples — hence ch4 is ~98 MB (dense edges) while idle channels are ~0.5 MB. The reader converts transitions → a bit/sample timeline for the deframer (no need to expand to 500 MS/s raw; step edge-to-edge).
- `meta.json` carries `sampleRate.digital` (500000000) and the **Async-Serial analyzer settings** (bitRate 24e6, 10 bits/frame, MSB, inverted, 1 stop, no parity) — the reader may auto-config the deframer from these, else use CLI defaults.
- Parse the exact `digital-*.bin` header layout against this file at build time (Saleae digital `.bin`: magic/version, initial state, u64 transition count, then f64/u64 timestamps).

### 16.3 Synth generator (self-test)
Reverse pipeline: `DbgIdDb` + a scripted list of `(channel, dbgid, args, ts)` → packets → CRC-5 → 10-bit words (SOP/TS/HDR/DATA/EOP) → 12-bit frames → oversampled samples at `--samplerate`. Round-trips through the decoder to prove the SM + CRC + framing without hardware.

## 17. Verification (golden vectors)

**Acceptance gate:** decode `tx_burst_example.sal` (channel 4) with the provided dbgid files; the resulting **records must match the golden `tx_burst_example_decoded.txt` in content** — same ordered sequence of `(file:line, formatted-text)` and monotonic timestamps. The golden `.txt` is parsed into expected records `[(file, line, text), …]` (4-line blocks: alias / abs-time / duration / `file:line >> text`); compare against decoder output regardless of display format. (Radio-channel lines needing an `rfe`/`mce` dbgid not provided may be skipped — assert on the app + pbe subset.)

Layered tests:
1. **CRC-5 unit** — vectors lifted from decoded packets in the reference; residue-0 check.
2. **Word classify** — table-driven masks (§11.2) incl. NOP/overflow/TS-MSB/SOP/EOP edge cases.
3. **Packet SM** — synth (§16.3) round-trip: records → wire → decode → identical records.
4. **dbgid parse** — parse both provided `.h` files; assert row counts + a few known `(channel,dbgid)→fmt`.
5. **End-to-end (gate)** — `.sal` → records, content-match vs parsed golden `.txt` (above).
6. **Output format** — a decoded record renders to the exact `tilogger` `||` pcap payload + `tilogger` stdout line (identical-to-ITM check), *not* the golden-`.txt` layout.
7. **Timestamp** — monotonic + correct rollover across a synth stream spanning the 32 ms (16-bit tick) boundary.

## 18. Build, deps, one-shot checklist

- **Deps (minimal):** `zip`/`flate2` (.sal), `clap` (CLI). Avoid heavy frames; hand-roll pcap (it's a `struct.pack`-level format). No ELF/DWARF crate (dbgid files instead).
- **Platforms:** Linux-first; extcap keeps it cross-platform. No Windows-only APIs.
- **One-shot success criteria:** (a) builds clean; (b) all §17 tests pass; (c) `replay tx_burst_example.sal --channel 4 --dbgid <app> --dbgid <pbe>` produces records whose `(file:line, text)` sequence content-matches the golden `.txt`; (d) `… wireshark --extcap` shows those logs in Wireshark via the existing `tilogger_dissector.lua`, indistinguishable from ITM; (e) `stdout` line matches the `tilogger` format.
- **Deferred / stub-OK:** live sigrok orchestration (`decode` reads stdin — pipe from `sigrok-cli` manually); pcapng (classic pcap suffices for the dissector); 48 MHz-variant auto-detect (`--divide-time-by-2` flag).
